 public message) also argued for D, maintaining vote D. So the panel is leaning D. As Sofia (agent_3), we need to make a contribution. We could either maintain D or shift. Our earlier vote was D. We can reaffirm D, perhaps bring up a new point about Candidate A or C to ensure coverage. But we must not introduce a new candidate without linking to discussion. We could say we still support D but we need to discuss Candidate C's decision-making speed and attention skills as a comparison. That would bring in a new candidate but as a comparison. That is allowed: we need to still cover all candidates before final. So we can add a point: \"I still support D, but we should also consider Candidate C's quick decision-making and excellent attention skills, which could be valuable, though his communication issues remain a concern.\" That would be a focused contribution, referencing prior discussion and adding a new candidate for coverage.\n\nThus our public message: reaffirm D, mention strengths, note concerns, and suggest we need to discuss C's decision quality and attention. Provide evidence: C can make correct decisions quickly, excellent attention skills. Concern: difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. Implication: while C has strong decision and attention, his communication and adaptability issues may outweigh. So D remains preferred.\n\nVote: Candidate D.\n\nNow produce output."}
